# Duplicate this file into Dialogues/ before editing.
# Replace TEMPLATE_NPC_ID everywhere with a unique ID, e.g. linh_yard.
# Replace NPC_NAME and all text inside <...>. Keep tabs for indentation.
# Completion below is a conversation choice, not a verified gameplay objective.

~ start
if GameState.npc_stage("TEMPLATE_NPC_ID") == "complete":
	=> completed
if GameState.npc_stage("TEMPLATE_NPC_ID") == "active":
	=> returning
=> first_meeting

~ first_meeting
set GameState.mark_met("TEMPLATE_NPC_ID")
NPC_NAME: <Greeting that shows this character's personality.> [#mood=happy]
NPC_NAME: <Explain the situation or give one useful clue.>
- <Player asks for more information.>
	NPC_NAME: <Answer the question.>
- <Player reacts or makes a joke.>
	NPC_NAME: <Respond in this character's voice.>
NPC_NAME: <Tell the player what to do next and where to go.>
set GameState.set_npc_stage("TEMPLATE_NPC_ID", "active")
=> END

~ returning
NPC_NAME: <Ask how things are going.>
- <Ask for the clue again.>
	NPC_NAME: <Repeat the next step clearly.>
	=> END
- <Finish this conversation thread.>
	NPC_NAME: <Acknowledge the player and offer a final tip.> [#mood=excited]
	set GameState.set_npc_stage("TEMPLATE_NPC_ID", "complete")
	=> END
- <Say goodbye.>
	=> END

~ completed
NPC_NAME: <Short line for later visits.>
=> END
